From 398c31c55e99cc62b48bb0891249b7873309f972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Garcia <44309076+ElGuslml@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 09:36:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: graphics pipelines linked from pipeline library parts

NativeXRenderer's patch for VK_EXT_graphics_pipeline_library (its D132). A
pipeline created with the new PSO_CREATE_FLAG_VK_LINK_FROM_LIBRARIES (and
PSO_CREATE_FLAG_ASYNCHRONOUS, with dynamic rendering, by an application that
enabled VK_KHR_pipeline_library and VK_EXT_graphics_pipeline_library through
EngineVkCreateInfo::ppDeviceExtensionNames and pDeviceExtensionFeatures) is
linked from four parts the device keeps: vertex input (the topology),
pre-rasterization shaders (the vertex shader's SPIR-V, the polygon mode, depth
clamp and viewport count), fragment shader (the pixel shader's SPIR-V) and
fragment output (the formats, samples and blending); the shader parts are keyed
with the pipeline's resource signatures, so pipelines with identically defined
layouts share them. The parts have the cull mode, front face, depth bias and
the depth-stencil state dynamic, so a part serves every such state; the context
sets them when it binds a linked pipeline
(CommandBuffer::SetLinkedPipelineDynamicState).

The linked pipeline is the PSO's at once; the whole pipeline, made as without
the flag, is compiled behind every other task (priority -1), its stages and
modules kept by the task, and replaces the linked one the next time the PSO is
set (PipelineStateVkImpl::PromoteWholePipeline from SetPipelineState; the
linked one released when the GPU is done with it). A pipeline that cannot be
linked (no parts, other stages, an input layout) is made whole. A PSO destroyed
before its whole pipeline takes the task out of the queue, or waits for it.

IRenderDeviceVk::GetPipelineLibraryStats counts the parts made and reused, the
pipelines linked, replaced and made whole.
